# =============================================================================
# Enterprise RAG Knowledge AI - environment template
# =============================================================================
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in real values:
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# There are deliberately NO `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables in this project. The
# browser never talks to the database or to OpenAI directly -- it only calls
# this app's own route handlers -- so every value below is server-side, and
# nothing here is inlined into the client bundle.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database (required)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRET. Any PostgreSQL 15+ with the `vector` extension available.
# Neon's free tier is the reference target; see README "Production Deployment".
#
# On Vercel, use Neon's **pooled** connection string (the host containing
# `-pooler`). A direct connection string will exhaust the free-tier connection
# limit once a few serverless instances are warm.
#
#   Neon:  postgresql://<user>:<password>@<endpoint>-pooler.<region>.aws.neon.tech/<db>?sslmode=require
#   Local: postgres://ragdev:ragdev@127.0.0.1:55433/ragdev
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI (required for embedding, OCR and answering)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRET. Server-side only; the browser never calls OpenAI directly.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-openai-api-key

# Chat model used for answer generation. Swappable without a code change.
# Reasoning models (o-series, gpt-5*) are detected automatically: they get
# `max_completion_tokens` with extra headroom and no custom temperature.
OPENAI_CHAT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Vision-capable model used only when a PDF page has no usable native text.
# OCR is page-scoped and is never run for pages that pass native extraction.
OPENAI_OCR_MODEL=gpt-5-mini

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public-demo abuse protection
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRET. Keys the HMAC that turns a visitor's IP into the anonymous fingerprint
# the demo quotas are counted against. Required in production.
#
# Why a secret and not a plain hash: the demo has no accounts, so a limit keyed
# on the session cookie is no limit at all -- clearing the cookie mints a new
# one. The counters are therefore keyed on the client instead. Storing
# `sha256(ip)` would not make that anonymous (the whole IPv4 space is only 2^32
# hashes, so anyone with the table could enumerate it); an HMAC under a key that
# never leaves the server cannot be reversed that way. No raw IP is ever stored.
#
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
#
# If it is unset the app still runs and still limits, but with a random
# per-instance secret: the counters do not survive a restart and are not shared
# between serverless instances. Fine for `npm run dev`, not for production.
DEMO_RATE_LIMIT_SECRET=generate-with-openssl-rand-hex-32

# Optional. Whether `x-forwarded-for` / `x-real-ip` may be believed.
#
# Left unset, they are trusted only when `VERCEL=1` -- i.e. on Vercel, whose
# edge overwrites whatever the client sent. Anywhere else a forwarded header is
# just a request header, and trusting it would be worse than having no limit,
# because a fresh value on every request would look like a fresh visitor.
#
# Set to 1 only if you run behind your own proxy that rewrites these headers.
# With no trusted header the app meters every request into a single shared
# bucket, which is correct for local development and fails closed elsewhere.
# DEMO_TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS=1

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAG tuning (all optional - defaults in src/lib/config/rag.ts)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Number of chunks retrieved per question.
RAG_TOP_K=5

# Minimum cosine similarity (0..1) for a chunk to count as relevant.
# Raise it for fewer, more precise citations; lower it for better recall.
RAG_SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD=0.45

# Chunk size / overlap in characters. Overlap is clamped to at most half the
# chunk size so the chunker can always advance.
RAG_CHUNK_SIZE=1000
RAG_CHUNK_OVERLAP=150

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Integration tests (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to run tests/integration/postgres.integration.test.ts against a real
# database. Point it at a throwaway/local instance, never at production: the
# suite applies migrations and writes rows.
# DATABASE_INTEGRATION_URL=postgres://ragdev:ragdev@127.0.0.1:55433/ragdev

# Set to 1 to run tests/integration/openai.integration.test.ts, which spends
# real OpenAI usage.
# RUN_OPENAI_INTEGRATION=1

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: The embedding model is intentionally NOT configurable here.
# text-embedding-3-small produces 1536-dimensional vectors, which is hard-coded
# in the `vector(1536)` column. Changing the model requires a database
# migration, not an environment variable.
#
# NOTE: There is no authentication configuration. This deployment is a public
# portfolio demo: visitors are separated by an anonymous demo-session cookie,
# not by accounts, and abuse is bounded by the fingerprint-scoped quotas above
# rather than by a login. See README "Security".
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
